On Tue, 2014-04-15 at 19:59 +0300, Samuli Sepp=C3=A4nen wrote:
> The driver has been tested on Windows 7 64-bit and it "seems to work
> ok". If you test this driver please let me know if it works - or if it
> does not.

I've finally got round to testing this with OpenConnect, also under
Windows 7 64-bit. It seems to be a little more pedantic about
DeviceIoControl() calls, and needs both input and output buffers to be
provided to all of them. So I needed to do this to make it work:
http://git.infradead.org/users/dwmw2/openconnect.git/commitdiff/c499aec29

Other than that, though, it seems to be working for both IPv6 and Legacy
IP.

With IPv6 I can't ping the other end of the VPN tunnel because I seem to
have a direct "on-link" route to that /64 network, rather than via
fe80::8. But I suspect that's probably a vpnc-script issue and not your
fault.

